#version 450
//! `y = tanh(x / cap) * cap`, Gemma's `final_logit_softcapping`.
//!
//! # Why an op and not an activation
//!
//! It carries a float. The activation path threads a `uint` code and, for `PRelu`, a tensor
//! index; a parameter would mean either a new push field on every convolution or overloading
//! `param0_bits`, which several kinds already use for something else. This runs **once** over the
//! logits at the end of a forward pass, not per layer, so a dedicated dispatch costs one pipeline
//! and no complexity anywhere else.
//!
//! # Why it cannot be folded away
//!
//! It is not a scale: `tanh` saturates. Dropping it changes which token wins whenever a logit
//! exceeds the cap, which is exactly the confident predictions - so a greedy decode diverges from
//! the reference on the tokens it is most sure about, and only on those.
//!
//! # Push fields
//!
//! `p.in0` is the input, `p.out_at` the output, `p.param0_bits` the cap as raw f32 bits, and
//! `p.count` the element count. Shapes are irrelevant: this is elementwise.

#include "common.glsl"

void main() {
    uint index = global_index();
    if (index >= p.count) {
        return;
    }
    float cap = uintBitsToFloat(p.param0_bits);
    arena[p.out_at + index] = float16_t(tanh(float(arena[p.in0 + index]) / cap) * cap);
}
